// act3_nineveh.ink
// Compile: npx inklecate -o data/dialogue/act3_nineveh.json data/dialogue/act3_nineveh.ink

-> city_gates

=== city_gates ===
The city is vast beyond reckoning — three days' journey across. Jonah walks in only one day's worth, and cries the word he was given.
"Yet forty days, and Nineveh shall be overthrown."
-> proclamation

=== proclamation ===
Word reaches the king before Jonah finishes speaking it twice.
He rises from his throne, lays his robe aside, covers himself with sackcloth, and sits in ashes.
A decree goes out: neither man nor beast, herd nor flock, shall taste anything. Let all cry mightily unto God. Let everyone turn from his evil way and the violence in his hands.
"Who can tell if God will turn and repent, and turn away from his fierce anger, that we perish not?"
-> jonah_watches

=== jonah_watches ===
The wave of repentance spreads through the streets below — an entire city, kneeling at once.
* [Watch]
    -> watch_response
* [Turn away]
    -> turn_away_response

=== watch_response ===
Jonah watches. Something in it unsettles him more than the storm did.
-> god_relents

=== turn_away_response ===
Jonah turns his back on the city before the wave even reaches the far wall.
-> god_relents

=== god_relents ===
And God saw their works, that they turned from their evil way; and God repented of the evil that he had said he would do unto them; and he did it not.
-> END
